### 5.5 Conclusion on JPMorgan: Accumulate on weakness

This is a high-quality franchise that is reasonably priced. The chart and the valuation both say the best entry is on weakness, not on strength. I would buy a first half of the intended position in the $316 to $326 zone (the 200-day averages and the pivot support), and the second half after a close above the 50-day average at $351.55 shows that the correction is over. If the stock closes below $315.70, I would stop and reassess.

